{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"SB0287","billNumberShort":"S.B. 287","billNumberLong":"SB0287S01","fileNumber":"2026FL1094","shortTitle":"Targeted Advertising Tax","currentSubVersion":"1","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"MCKELMK","primeSponsorName":"Sen. McKell, Michael K.","primeSponsorHouse":"S","floorSponsor":"TEUSCJ","floorSponsorName":"Rep. Teuscher, Jordan D.","floorSponsorHouse":"H","generalProvisions":"This bill imposes a tax on targeted advertising in the state.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>defines terms;<hr><ltbullet>imposes an annual tax on entities that deliver targeted advertising in Utah and meet certain revenue thresholds, based on the entity's gross receipts from targeted advertising in the state;<hr><ltbullet>requires entities subject to the tax to annually remit a return to the State Tax Commission that includes information related to the tax;<hr><ltbullet>provides for administration and collection of the tax by the State Tax Commission;<hr><ltbullet>provides rulemaking authority to the State Tax Commission for administration of the tax;<hr><ltbullet>establishes the Targeted Advertising Restricted Account (restricted account) for the deposit of tax revenue;<hr><ltbullet>provides for the use of money deposited into the restricted account; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Gus Harb","fiscalAnalyst":"Andrea Wilko","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/25/2026","trackingID":"XUFFOTLJOH","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-02-10 14:43:56.070","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and